// The 932 elementary Munsell blocks that define the 267 level-3 ISCC-NBS categories.
//
// Source: the "Color Name Charts" of NBS Special Publication 440, via
// bstreiff/iscc-nbs-colors (CC0-1.0). Requires color.cql to have been run first.
//
// Each block is a half-open box in Munsell space -- hue x value x chroma. A category
// is the union of its blocks; non-rectangular regions in the charts are decomposed
// into several adjacent boxes, so a category may own up to a few dozen.
//
// Bounds are half-open, [begin, end). An unbounded upper edge (printed as 'INF' in the
// source, where the chart runs off the top of the page) is stored as a MISSING property,
// so test it with 'IS NULL' or fold it away with coalesce(block.chromaEnd, 1e9).
//
// Hue is both the chart label ('1R') and its position on the normalized hue circle in
// 0..1 ('hueBeginAmount'). The 31 hue ranges are contiguous and close into a full circle,
// numbered in chart order by 'hueIndex' starting at 1R. Exactly one range -- 4R..6R,
// hueIndex 1 -- wraps the 0/1 seam, so hueBeginAmount > hueEndAmount there. Compare on
// hueIndex rather than on the amounts unless you handle that wrap yourself.

UNWIND [
